# Ignore everything, then allow the few things this branch is: the document, the pointer, and this
# file. Output, the package copy, the tree's own metadata, cargo's target, the demo's build — all of
# it falls under the first rule, which is the point: what the tool produces is the document's
# business, and a list there would have to be maintained here.
*
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/lp.typ

# Temporary: the notes are still tracked on this branch. They move to their own branch and take
# these two exceptions with them — until then, without them, `git add` would silently skip a new note.
!/agent-notes/
!/agent-notes/**

# The exception above re-includes everything under agent-notes/, including what the probes build and
# generate. Those stay out; the rule has to come after the exception to win.
/agent-notes/**/target/
/agent-notes/**/out/
/agent-notes/**/*.pdf
/agent-notes/**/*.png
